    {
      "id": "2125093341322940798",
      "text": "It's a 7-0 run for the Lakers to start the 4th Q with Doncic resting on the bench, capped by a transition 3 from Sexton, pushing the lead back to 8.",
      "url": "https://x.com/LakersReporter/status/2125093341322940798",
      "published": "2026-11-24T05:05:09+00:00",
      "likes": 175,
      "author": "Mike Trudell",
      "handle": "LakersReporter",
      "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/524367536763056130/32h6Ng8Y_normal.jpeg",
      "media": "",
      "quoted_text": "",
      "quoted_author": "",
      "quoted_handle": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "2125091874390290698",
      "text": "After allowing 42 points in the 1st half, LA conceded 35 in the 3rd Q, and saw their 11-point lead trimmed to one going into the 4th Q. Doncic has 24 points (8 of 23 FG's, 3 of 13 3's) with 7 assists, with Jake LaRavia (12 points) the only other Laker in double figures.",
      "url": "https://x.com/LakersReporter/status/2125091874390290698",
      "published": "2026-11-24T04:59:19+00:00",
      "likes": 84,
      "author": "Mike Trudell",
      "handle": "LakersReporter",
      "avatar": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/524367536763056130/32h6Ng8Y_normal.jpeg",
